 "result": "**Where to look:** `src/tessel/wrappers.py:181` (`Request.bundles`), which feeds `_pick_fault_handler` through `route_http_fault` (`src/tessel/app.py:860`).\n\n**Why:**\n- `route_http_fault` calls `_pick_fault_handler(e, ctx.request.bundles)`, and `_pick_fault_handler` (`sansio/app.py:878`) only searches `(*bundles, None)`.\n- `Request.bundles` is derived from the matched endpoint's bundle. Its docstring says it returns an empty list \"if URL matching failed\".\n- For an unknown URL, routing raises `NotFound` before any endpoint is matched, so `bundles == []`. The lookup then only checks app-level handlers (`None`), and your bundle's 404 handler is never consulted.\n- With no app-level 404 handler either, `route_http_fault` returns the raw exception, which is the default 404 page.\n\n**Fix:** register the 404 handler on the app, not the bundle. A bundle 404 handler only fires when a view in that bundle raises `abort(404)`. If you need per-bundle 404 pages for unmatched URLs, use an app-level handler that inspects `request.path` and dispatches to the right bundle's handling.",
